I'll add the repro tests to `game/neon.test.js` to follow TDD.
Actually, I should just fix D1 first.

The logic for D1 is:
When `collides(ball, brick)` is true:
1. Determine which face was hit.
2. Flip the corresponding velocity component.
3. Reposition the ball to be exactly on the edge of the brick.

How to determine the face?
Calculate the overlap on each axis. The axis with the smallest overlap is the one we collided on.

```javascript
const overlapX = Math.min(ball.x + ball.r - brick.x, brick.x + brick.w - (ball.x - ball.r));
const overlapY = Math.min(ball.y + ball.r - brick.y, brick.y + brick.h - (ball.y - ball.r));

if (overlapX < overlapY) {
  // Side collision
  ball.vx = -ball.vx;
  // Reposition
  if (ball.x + ball.r < brick.x + brick.w / 2) {
    ball.x = brick.x - ball.r;
  } else {
    ball.x = brick.x + brick.w + ball.r;
  }
} else {
  // Top/Bottom collision
  ball.vy = -ball.vy;
  // Reposition
  if (ball.y + ball.r < brick.y + brick.h / 2) {
    ball.y = brick.y - ball.r;
  } else {
    ball.y = brick.y + brick.h + ball.r;
  }
}
```

